Hello D-I porters,

Most architectures should now be able to switch to 2.6.20 for D-I (except=20
for arm, hppa and m68k). i386 and amd64 have already been switched.

Over the past two weeks Joey has done the needed work for i386 and amd64=20
(and necessary updates in kernel-wedge), but we've waited with this call=20
until #419458 was resolved (which it was in 2.6.20-3).

As this is a fairly big jump (2.6.18 to 2.6.20), please check carefully=20
for new modules that should be included in the udebs. If any updates in=20
kernel-wedge are needed, please let us know (or do them yourself).
I suggest that you check the kernel-wedge changelog for an overview of the=
=20
changes made there.

Please also check pending changes already committed in SVN by Joey or me.

Note that although new PATA modules were added in kernel-wedge, most of=20
these are not actually available yet in the kernel as a result of=20
#419458.

After you upload the new linux-kernel-* package, I will make sure that the=
=20
linux-modules-* (loop-aes modules) will also be uploaded for your=20
architecture.

=46or mips(el):
In input-modules for bcm* kernels, usbmouse is currently included. AFAIK=20
that module should not be needed and that module could be removed.

