I'd like to monitor the sensors on a CS20. I've seen hwmon-1.0.3.tar.gz,
which contains a bunch of i2c sensors modules, but they haven't been updated
for kernel 2.6.

It seems that some/all of those modules are now in 2.6 (adm9240 and lm75,
most notably). When I insert adm9240 and lm75, I get:

i2c_adapter i2c-0: found ADM9240 revision 2
i2c_adapter i2c-0: Error: device error
i2c_adapter i2c-0: Idle wait Timeout! STS=0x00
i2c_adapter i2c-0: SMBus Timeout!
i2c_adapter i2c-0: Idle wait Timeout! STS=0x00
i2c_adapter i2c-0: SMBus Timeout!

sensors-detect(8) gives

Probing for PCI bus adapters...
Use driver `i2c-ali15x3' for device 0000:00:11.0: Acer Labs 1533/1543
Use driver `i2c-ali1535' for device 0000:00:11.0: Acer Labs 1535
[snip]
Next adapter: SMBus ALI15X3 adapter at 1040
Do you want to scan it? (YES/no/selectively): 
[nothing found]

I modprobed for these two modules, but sensors(1) still yields:

No sensors found!
Make sure you loaded all the kernel drivers you need.
Try sensors-detect to find out which these are.

thanks,
john
